A||||32||Joe4x4||I got hit....||||8||
Z||000000||Joe4x4||06-04-2001||11:53 AM||||It is monday 5am we stop at the local food store (Acme). We park in center lane (right side)5 cars down. There is maybe 8 cars in the whole parking lot (big lot). I did see the car that hit sitting there (no knowing that I would be chasing  this car down in 5 min), and there was this guy sitting in his car grabing a smoke (I figured he was on his brake...worked for the store ).<P>OK.....so we go in find nothing that we want so we decide to head home and I would had my left over pizza and she would have her left over chicken.<BR>As we are at the exit 10 feet from the exit doors we hear my car alarm going of (I`m thinking can`t pepole park without hitting my car) WRONG.......This Big Caddy is going fast to my right (leaving fast I thought).<P>The guy that was out there grabing a smoke <BR>YEALS.....THEY JUST HIT YOUR CAR.....<BR>I was no way , they hit my car and don`t stop and get out,.....(I WAS HOT)<BR>I told my girl get in ...THE CHASE.<BR>So we start the car ,I go the way they <BR>left the parking lot, get to the street<BR>left or right?<BR>traffic light red to the left &gt;&gt;&gt;we go right<BR>next intercesion 50 feet....straight  or right left ????? look left no cars<BR>look straight no cars...look right see <BR>the tail lights of that Big Caddy...YES<P>Hit the gas ......I got up on there butt<BR>(I see alot of heads in the car).<BR>I`m thinking Ohh ..Ohh  wish I had a Cell Phone. We stay back hoping we come across<BR>a cop. Never find one when you need one.<BR>They go into a housing complex..Ohh Ohh<BR>thinking this is not looking good.<BR>(not in a Bad section)<BR>They pull into a parking spot.I came up to that Big Caddy from behind ....looking at the car people inside...the driver`s door<BR>opened (my car was running and in gear).<P>A Japanise lady 5`2" tall gets out...<BR>I yeall at her ..YOU HIT MY CAR AND YOU JUST <BR>TAKE OFF !!!!<P>She says woe woe....then she goes to the caddy passenger side rear out cames a young <BR>man in his 20`s. He goes she does not speak English ...I tell the same thing I told her <BR>and he says she did not hit my car she hit a shopping cart...I was getting HOTTER..<BR>than a third head came out the Caddy  (lady 2), and was saying ...(she no hit you...no damage..no)<BR>Lady 2 was saying to call the cops .I said call the cops I`ll be back in 10 min...<BR>I wan`t to go back to the Acme  and get the Eye witness before he left (did not know if he worked there are not at the time).<P>I got back to the store ,the car was still there..then we knew he was a worker getting  <BR>a smoke at the time.We went inside told the casher what happend (she knows us we stop there alot after work). Frank the eye wittnes<BR>said she backed into the back of the fiero, <BR>and when she did he saw her head go back and then forward.(20 feet distance between cars)<BR>He said he saw that Big Caddy rock back and forth, and then she put in drive and took off<BR>like a bat out of hell.<P>That was when the chase started. We called the police they came out , we told them what happened we gave them the licence plate #<BR>where we followed them to. they took a report and now we have to wait for the police report ,She is going to get a sumens <BR>in the mail. The cop said ..(you followed them?)<BR>I said yea....I know..I was playing it smart<BR>I told the cop, he just looked at me.<P>The thing is, there was no damage that I could she ..I see where she hit me (car a little dirty at the time).<P>But since she decided to take off ,and be a *****  about this..I wounded what damage she might have done to my fiero....like The hit broke my dog bone that caused to brake the block..$$$  or the hit broke the tranny $$$<BR>or the hit broke the suspension ..$$$.<P>What do you guys think I should do??<P><P>------------------<BR>Need For Speed........<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/car1.gif"> ||||reg||8
Z||000001||saleenfiero||06-04-2001||12:31 PM||||The hell of it is, since you chased the people down, the cops will lecture you about calling them first and not taking things into your own hands, I'd have done the same thing because around here, our cops are useless.  I don't know the next course of action, but I'd say get a damage estimate and sue her into the ground.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Joe4x4||06-04-2001||12:50 PM||||Yea that is what I want to do get a HIGH estame...make them pay .<P>thanks||||reg||1
Z||000003||stsmithgt||06-04-2001||01:29 PM||||I Hate! it when they pull the ol' "I don't speak english shi--!"   I'd have it checked out and drive that Goo..."person" into the ground with a lawsuit and make sure she gets charged with a "hit and run" ticket to deal with.  She should cover all costs that relate to the incident.||||reg||4
Z||000004||ThatRickGuy||06-04-2001||01:51 PM||||Look for any kind of damage you can find, take the car to a frame shop and see if it's bent, get the alignment checked, make sure the impact absorbers aren't damaged, check all the mounts and pop the hood and have somebody watch the engine when you put it in gear to see if the engine shifts excessively. Nail her for what ever you can, I'm a firm beleive that incompetent people should not be alloud to drive.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Ken Wittlief||06-04-2001||01:58 PM||||you need to check out your bumper and stuff underneight. The plastic outer covering will dent and pop back out - but underneight it could be all crumpled.<P>  I knew a guy who took his new saturn to the dealer - he couldnt roll the drivers door window down.<P>  turns out someone had smacked the door and bent the crash protection bar into the window mechanism - but the plastic side panel popped back out with hardly a scratch.<P>  so he doesnt even know when the car was hit or where.||||reg||1
Z||000006||rogergarrison||06-04-2001||02:10 PM||||THey could have told you on the lot, that they were sorry and they hit you. Since they took off, ill bet they had no idea how much damage they did, they could have done a lot. I had my Mercedes hit in a parking lot and done $3000 in damage. I say throw the book at them, at very least have them cited for leaving the scene. Here thats a $1000 fine or loss of your license. Thats the trouble anymore, no one has any respect for anyone elses property.||||reg||1
Z||000007||87GT||06-04-2001||07:49 PM||||Its amazing how pathetic people can be.  Trash somebody's personal property and take off.  I hope you bust them good!!||||reg||1
Z||000008||isthiswhereiputausername?||06-04-2001||08:14 PM||||make sure you get the highest estimates to fix  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><BR>Someone hit my wifes Tempest, (front drivers side bumped cracked and pushed down a few inches) We didnt notice it til a few days ago when we were waxing it..   I love when people stop and admit what they do.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Hank is Here||06-04-2001||08:33 PM||||Best way to get a higher estimate with being 100% completly honest is clean the car up the best you can except the area that got hit.  Body shops tipically give higher estimates to nice cars and not beaters.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Ed||06-04-2001||08:51 PM||||Go look at "THUMPED" in the archives from about May 23.<P>Another hit and run, but a witness got a description and the culprit has been located. No insurance.  Third week now and my car is parked in the garage.  $4,000 to $6,000 in damage.  I expect to get $3500 minmum to repair it (I will repair it if possible, as its replacement value, to me at least, is worth it) under my uninsured property damge provisions.  Highway Patrol report is not out yet so I don't know the responsibility of the first person in line who STOPPED IN THE TRAFFIC LANE TO LOOK AT SOMETHING!  ||||reg||1
Z||000011||rogergarrison||06-05-2001||12:17 AM||||Ca has uninsured property damage? I may be wrong, but I think that uninsured insurance only covers personal injury. I know thats the way it is in ohio. You would have to claim in under your collision and pay the deductable. Check before you send your car out. If you dont carry coll, your SOL.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Joe4x4||06-05-2001||02:16 AM||||Let`s see gonna go to a frame shop $$,body shop $$,engine shop $$,and I wounder if I take my car to a head doctor (for cars)$$ <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.<BR>ThatRickGuy....Ken Wittlief........(1)<P>Ticket for leaving the sceane of a accident.<BR>I`m gonna teach her A$$ !!!<BR>rogergarrison........(2)<P>Clean the Fiero...that is very good idea <BR>before going for the estimates.<BR>Hank is Here......(3)<P>Sorry to hear about your car...ED. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">.<P>Thanks for advice...I`ll keep you guys <BR>posted .....Lets see what we can get this <BR>B!tch to play, and learn a lession.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000013||Ken Wittlief||06-05-2001||08:57 AM||||Now that you have had a day or two to cool off a couple of things to keep in mind<P>maybe this sounds silly but keep your karma in mind (or whatever you want to call it)<P>it is possible the people in the other car thought these cars all have 5mph bumpers... maybe they really thought bumping in a parking lot would do no real damage (even if its stupidity on their part - there is a difference between being stupid and being irresponsible)<P>the other thing to keep in mind, someday you might be on the other end of a minor accident - and as they say, what goes around...  sometimes even when an accident is not your fault, its still your fault.<P>Yes get your car fixed and fixed right. <P>Yes they pay for the damages.<P>And remember your true character is revealed in difficult situations. A little kindness and understanding on your part now will come back to you when YOU need it the most.||||reg||1
Z||000014||stsmithgt||06-05-2001||10:03 AM||||Karma Shmarma. (bitter boy coming through) I've been nice to people all my life and alls I've got out of it is my wallet being emptied one way or nother.  Throw the book at here.  If she thinks she's a victom, she stupid.  If she's smart she'll learn her lesson not to hit and run ANYTHING.  That includes animals.  I had a pure breed german shepard run over by a post man who hit and ran. ($1000.00 gone) Lucky he did, I had a .45 on my side at the time out on the farm, but that's another story. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000015||fiero56||06-05-2001||10:56 AM||||<B>(even if its stupidity on their part - there is a difference between being stupid and being irresponsible)</B><P>Ignorance is no excuse for breaking the law. Ask any cop. Being stupid is no excuse either.||||reg||1
Z||000016||Ken Wittlief||06-05-2001||11:39 AM||||As much as we all love and pamper our metal and plastic machines, I am pretty sure that leaving the scene of an accident is only a crime if someone is injured.<P>  If you tap someones bumper do you have to stay there till the cops show up?<P>  If you only touch bumpers? Is that considered an accident?!<P>  If you smack it good but dont see any damage?<P>   Nobody here has ever parallel parked and touched the car behind them? One mans touch is another mans 'creamed'.<P>   all Im saying is maybe<P>    Maybe!<P>   they didnt realize they did any damage.<P>  and maybe the next time you are standing there filling out an accident report with the police, maybe the other person will be screaming at you, or your wife, or GF, or daughter - threathening you with the lawsuit.||||reg||1
Z||000017||Ed||06-05-2001||01:11 PM||||For Rogergarrison and others:<P>I got lucky, or maybe I had some forethought, but my policy does have a provision called "uninsured property damage."  Yes, uninsured motorist is for injuries, but this covers the car. In brief, WHEN (this case) an uninsured motorist hits me, I'm covered for $3,500 or the actual cash value of the car (whichever is less). So it will work out as being about the same as if I kept my collision coverage.<P>AAA of southern CA has a website which describes the various coverages, at least in CA. (I'm in no. CA but I have AAA, similar)<P>Now, Joe4x4, we have to play out the game.  It's going into the third week and now my alternator's bearing is giving up.  I'm not going to fix that until I know if the body can be repaired. So now, no car, and no end immediately in sight.  <P>Another joker in my case, is whether the first guy in line is found to have any responsibility for the accident.  If he does, my $3,500 will be reduced percentage-wise, and I'll have to deal with the first guy's insurance company. <P>I agree with other comments, though, you don't know the mindset of the person who hit you.  Just play out the insurance game and recover what you can.  <P>As Joe Bob Briggs says, "Life is like a horror movie, something bad can happen at any time."  <P>These accidents aren't those.  Just minor inconveniences. ||||reg||1
Z||000018||Coop88||06-05-2001||01:23 PM||||Can the police really do anything? I remember when my brother's neon got nailed buy some kid trying to show off to his friends how fast he could drive in reverse. The kid didn't have any registration, or even a license. It hit hard enough to cause a little over $3000 in damage. The cop said nothing could be done since it happened on private property(White Castle parking lot). Not a ticket or anything. He also said it was a good thing my brother had uninsured motorists ins. That's why you will always see my car at the very end of the parking lot-far from everyone else.||||reg||1
Z||000019||Ken Wittlief||06-05-2001||01:44 PM||||"That's why you will always see my car at the very end of the parking lot-far from everyone else."<P>weellllllllllllllll not always good<P>sometimes that means they get going faster before they hit you. :0<P>statistically 25% of all drivers are involved in some kind of accident with damage during their driving years.<P>which is about a million times more likely than winning the lottery -<P>  most people will buy lottery tickets and think they have a least some chance of winning<P>  but when their car gets hit its like this is the first time in the history of mankind that two motor vehicles ever collided "How could this happen?!"<P>   One out of four people - are there four people in your home that drive / will drive?<P>   this stuff happens all over the place every day - you gotta expect it. Its not unusual, its normal. ||||reg||1
Z||000020||Ed||06-05-2001||02:43 PM||||Update:<P>I was just lucky.  Calif. law requires this uninsured property damage coverage, unless you actively waive it.  <P>On mindset: The person who hit me was on the way to see her daughter, who started labor pains.  She was using someone else's car.  Didn't know if it was insured.  Daughter was okay so she was going back home, when the car quit because the radiator had been damaged. <P>Would you have stopped if your daughter was starting labor?  Was she so poor she couldn't afford a car?  (I think there should be a tax at the gas pump for minimum insurance.  You don't need insurance or a license to drive a car, you do need gasoline) Now, she's wrecked someone else's car besides.  She could have phoned in, but maybe she was so stressed out she didn't think of it.<P>So even though I'm really unhappy my beautiful car was whacked, I think she probably is in a worse situation.||||reg||1
Z||000021||rogergarrison||06-05-2001||04:03 PM||||In ohio, Ken, anytime you hit anything, even a street sign post, if you leave without reporting it-thats a crime-leaving the scene of an accident. 2 from my own experience. I was making a left turn at a busy intersection and a car coming towards me touched, not hit a rubber bumper cover on a t bird I was driving. No one in the car even felt it and I went to my destination down the street. Well the guy that touched me must have known because he pulled over in a shopping center and called police on me. I was surprized to see a group of police cars pull in and start looking over my car. sure enough there was a scratch on my bumper cover and a stripe like a pencil line running down the side of his car-my car color. I had to go to court and risk losing my license for leaving the scene. Luckily I had a picture of my car to show the judge and witnesses that didnt know the cars had even touched. With that, he let me go with a ticket for failure to yield on left turn.<P>other one was a lady who backed into a street name sign across from her driveway. She ended up calling the city to replace the sign. She should have kept her mouth shut, because she had to pay a fine for leaving the scene, and something like $800 for labor and sign to be replaced.||||reg||1
Z||000022||Ken Wittlief||06-05-2001||04:25 PM||||the one thing about accidents that drives me right up the wall is when two cars get into a minor fender bender, and nobody is hurt, and they keep their cars right there where the bump happened, in the middle lane of the thruway, or in the middle of a 4 lane by 4 lane intersection in the middle of rush hour<P>   as if the police are gonna come and photograph the scene and measure skid marks for $200 worth of bent sheet metal<P>  they are backing up rush hour traffic for 4 miles in 4 directions - making 20,000 commuters crawl along at 3 mph for an hour.<P>   Maybe Im wrong on this one, but if nobody requires the jaws of life, get your cars OFF the pavement and bicker with each other over whos fault it is when the cops arrive.<P>   The cops cant tell what happened from where your car comes to a stop, and its your word against the other guys in the end anyway.<P>   It must be some psychological disorder with our society. you can put a piece of metal in a vice and bend it back and forth and wack it with a hammer all day and nobody gets upset.<P>   But if a piece of metal is attached to someones car, and it gets bent, you would think their firstborn son had been slain.<P>   maybe someday society will resign itself to the fact that you cant have 100,000,000 cars driving around in north america with out them bumping into each other, and will start designing cars more like bumper cars.<P>  one less thing to have an anurism over.||||reg||1
Z||000023||Ed||06-05-2001||04:53 PM||||Well, Ken, take heart that I suggested we get out of the traffic lane, and did.  Took down all the info while the CHP was enroute.  Everything after the accident went the way it was supposed to, and nobody shot at each other like the unfortunate incident in this area a couple of weeks ago.  <P>People got mad at a "cut off".  One guy shot the other dead.  Then a week later he killed himself out of remorse.  Two people dead, and families affected over nothing.||||reg||1
Z||000024||Mach10||06-05-2001||06:02 PM||||*D-Oh!*<p>[This message has been edited by Mach10 (edited 06-05-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000025||Mach10||06-05-2001||06:05 PM||||Saw a little white sprint drift, on ice, into the back of a huge newer crown vic. Both hop out. And start exchanging details. This is in the middle of a curbed on-ramp. There's no way around 'em. I'm late for school, and it's rushhour. I stick my head out and ask them if they could roll up about 25ft to let traffic through. The huge gorrilla in the Vic roars at me that they'd just been in an accident. I hop out, and act all concerned.<BR>"Omigod! Is anyone hurt?"<BR>"Uh... No."<BR>"Are both cars still running?"<BR>"What? What the hell do you think? Yeah!"<BR>"So no-one's hurt, and both cars are mobile.<BR>GET YOUR STUPID ASS OUT OF THE WAY, YOU'RE HOLDING US UP!"<P>I don't know why I keep getting into confrontations with people larger than me. It's a character flaw. I've been lucky so far, they usually back down  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>As for this incident, I've always been an honest bastard, so yeah, I'd go get the damages checked out, but I wouldn't exagerate things. I've hit some people and have been told not to worry about minor damage, so I wouldn't go hounding after someone 'cos the door flew open in the wind and put a ding in my door. However, leaving the scene demands at least the ticket. Nail the cowards. Nail 'em to the wall.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000026||grinthock||06-05-2001||07:13 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fiero56:<BR><B>[b](even if its stupidity on their part - there is a difference between being stupid and being irresponsible)</B><P>Ignorance is no excuse for breaking the law. Ask any cop. Being stupid is no excuse either.[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>No offense to anyone asian.  But here in Canada some foreign'r pulls that I don't speak english ****  in court and the judge lets them off saying "Yes in this country you can't do that, have a nice day" with me it's "You are a young a$$ who thought you were a hot shot, you are gonna burn"<P>And people wonder why I hate our immigration system.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000027||87GTBro||06-05-2001||09:03 PM||||Sounds like it is time for a new paint job and rebuilt engine on Big Caddy ladies tab!!!||||reg||1
Z||000028||Ken Wittlief||06-05-2001||11:50 PM||||I was in a minor incident about a year ago in my 94 saturn SL2. I was waiting at a red light to make a right on red, and was about half way around the corner.<P>  a lady pulled up behind me, to do the same thing. Im watching the traffic to my left thinking, maybe, no, not enough time to pull out (i was being conservative)<P>  I got the car in 1st and my foot lightly on the brake, and all of a sudden the car starts going around the corner.<P>   Im thinking, "what the H#LL?!"<P>   the lady behind me though I had already gone, and was looking to her left too, and had creeped right up on my bumper, and started to go - never bothered to look and see what was infront of her.<P>   she only pushed me about 8 feet before we both stopped. when I realized what had happened I started laughing.<P>  I didnt even bother to get out of the car, i just waved her on.<P>   so technically we both were guilty of fleeing the scene of an accident?!<P>   when I washed the car a few days later there was a little bit of a scuff mark on my white bumper - a little Comet took it right off.<P>   it all happened so unexpectantly  - it really is a funny / odd feeling when your car starts taking off on you, when you have your foot on the brake. For a few seconds there I had no idea what was going on - oh no, tractor beam!||||reg||1
Z||000029||Joe4x4||06-06-2001||03:13 PM||||I just went out side ...some pics<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Jun06$01.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Jun06$02.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Jun06$05.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Jun06$06.jpg"> <P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000030||fiero56||06-06-2001||03:26 PM||||<B>the one thing about accidents that drives me right up the wall is when two cars get into a minor fender bender, and nobody is hurt, and they keep their cars right there where the bump happened, </B><P>This happened to a friend. He was rear-ended by a guy probably in his 40s. The guy told him to move his car into a nearby parking lot so they wouldn't block traffic. Somehow the guy who rear ended my friend, conviced the cops it was my friend who caused the accident, and somehow rear-ended himself. My friend got slapped with the reapir bills for both cars, court costs, pain&suffering(neck pain???), etc. Ever since that happened, if I ever get rear-ended I will block 30,000 commuters at 5 o'clock if I have to until the cops arrive. That, and I now always have a camera in my cars too.||||reg||1
Z||000031||87GTBro||06-06-2001||03:30 PM||||I Have an Idea!!!<P>Jump in the bronco there in the background and drive over to the ladies house and make a pancake out of that big old caddy!!!  <P>She'll never know it was you that did it!!!  Who would think that a Fiero could drive over a cadillac???<P>No, seriously, there could be serious damage to the honeycomb underneath your bumper.  By looking at the decklid, she may have bent the frame a little.  You should have it looked at...  She should buy you a new bumper too... It is hard to permanently fix a crack like that...  They tend to keep surfacing when fixed....  IMHO...||||reg||1
Z||000032||stsmithgt||06-06-2001||03:32 PM||||DAMN! It moved your lid?  Shopping cart my @$$.  She's a criminal technically.  Use the full extent of the law.  Ask lots of questions.  Police and lawyers don't give out as much info. as they know without being asked.  The hinge as well as the lid itself could be screwed up.  Good luck.  This cituation isn't fun in my book.  Too many times the criminal is let off the hook.||||reg||4
